; Tagged types (`#6.n(...)`).
; - A bare top-level `tagged = #6.42(text)` is a single-type tag wrapper of a primitive. It AUTO-WRAPS
;   into a tag-writing/tag-checking newtype: serialize writes `write_tag(42)` then the inner value, and
;   deserialize rejects a wrong tag with `DeserializeFailure::TagMismatch`. A transparent `pub type` can
;   physically not carry a custom impl, so the only way its OWN standalone `to/from_cbor_bytes` API can
;   honor the tag is to emit a real newtype wrapper — hence auto-wrap is the default (a deliberate
;   breaking change from the earlier `pub type Tagged = String`, which silently dropped the tag from the
;   standalone wire API — a CBOR conformance bug).
; - `tagged_newtype = #6.42(text) ; @newtype` requests the same wrapper via the comment DSL. Auto-wrap
;   makes `@newtype` REDUNDANT on a tag rule (not a double wrapper): `tagged` and `tagged_newtype`
;   generate byte-identical wrapper shapes — the snapshots pin that equivalence.
; - `holder` references `tagged_newtype` so the embed role compiles; embedded and standalone both write
;   the tag.
tagged = #6.42(text)
tagged_newtype = #6.42(text) ; @newtype
holder = [payload: tagged_newtype]
